Rawimage.mcc/Rawimage.mcc
Rawimage.mcc/MUIA_Rawimage_Data
Rawimage.mcc/Rawimage.mcc

    NAME
        Rawimage.mcc -- Display embedded raw or compressed images.

    SUPERCLASS
        Pixmap.mui

    DESCRIPTION
        Convert an embedded MUI_RawimageData header into Pixmap attributes.
        Supported ARGB and RGB payloads are raw, BZip2 and RLE. Z and LZMA
        format identifiers are declared but not implemented.

    NOTES
        All four header ULONG fields use big-endian byte order, even on i386.
        Pixel bytes are ARGB or RGB. The image payload is borrowed, not copied;
        keep it readable and unchanged for the object's lifetime.
        On construction, invalid non-NULL data causes object creation to fail.
        After construction, the setter does not report translation or decode
        errors. Recreate the object rather than replacing its live payload:
        Pixmap may retain cached data or mishandle previously borrowed buffers.
        Neither class fully validates malformed image data.

    SEE_ALSO
        MUIA_Rawimage_Data, Pixmap.mui
Rawimage.mcc/MUIA_Rawimage_Data

    NAME
        MUIA_Rawimage_Data -- Supply embedded image data.

    FUNCTION
        Set Pixmap dimensions, pixel format, compression and payload.

    INPUTS
        Initialize/set; struct MUI_RawimageData *. No local getter.
        ri_Width, ri_Height, ri_Format and ri_Size are big-endian ULONGs.
        ri_Data follows the 16-byte header. For raw data, ri_Size may be zero.

    NOTES
        Supported formats: RAWIMAGE_FORMAT_RAW_ARGB_ID,
        RAWIMAGE_FORMAT_RAW_RGB_ID, RAWIMAGE_FORMAT_BZ2_ARGB_ID,
        RAWIMAGE_FORMAT_BZ2_RGB_ID, RAWIMAGE_FORMAT_RLE_ARGB_ID,
        and RAWIMAGE_FORMAT_RLE_RGB_ID. Supply valid dimensions,
        lengths and readable, suitably aligned persistent storage.
        GetTagData uses the first Data tag. NULL does not clear an image.
        On Set, the wrapper ignores the conversion result and forwards the
        original tags; other Pixmap tags can override translated settings.
        The payload remains caller-owned. No rollback is guaranteed on error.

    EXAMPLE
        One opaque red ARGB pixel, as bytes (not native ULONG constants):
        00 00 00 01  00 00 00 01  00 00 00 00  00 00 00 00
        ff ff 00 00
        Store at a suitably aligned address for the object's lifetime.

    SEE_ALSO
        Rawimage.mcc, MUIA_Pixmap_Data

